{{number box|fr}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|fr|tri-|gloss1=three|-illion}}, from {{m|fr|million}}; [[i.e.]] a [[million]] [[million]] [[million]].

Coined by {{w|Jehan Adam}} in 1475 as '''trimillion'''.<!--<ref name="genevieve" /> <ref name="parchemin" /> <ref name="thorndike" />-->
Rendered as '''tryllion''' by {{w|Nicolas Chuquet}} in 1484, in his article “Triparty en la science des nombres”.<!--<ref name="Chuquet1" /> <ref name="Chuquet2" />-->

